[
  {
    "sha": "de5829e8fd688a58bad76fd1338ea135c23c2921",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGRlNTgyOWU4ZmQ2ODhhNThiYWQ3NmZkMTMzOGVhMTM1YzIzYzI5MjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:11:55Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:11:55Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui,mcp): work offsets listed by the setup's post; MCP takes an index\n\nThe Setups page combo lists offsets 1..=max of the setup's own post,\nworded \"Work offset n (NAME)\" (\"Work offset n\" when the post names\nnone); a stored pick beyond the post's range stays visible as itself\nand says so. The heights hint and the combo's hover no longer name a\nfixed G54-G59 range.\n\nMCP set_work_offset takes a 1-based index (G54-G59 as aliases of 1-6;\nword kept as the older spelling), refused by setup name through the\ncommand's own post check. Replies, set_wcs and get_job carry index and\nname, with word kept as an alias of name. camcraft-mcp skill updated;\nPROCESS_VERSION 21.\n\nSlice 3 of 3, stacked on #1113.\n\nFixes #931\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
